"{\"requirement\": \"The modern armchair has a rounded, ergonomic design with a slightly depressed seat cushion for comfort. The backrest curves smoothly for support, and the armrests are short and curved, positioned for elbow rest. Four straight, square wooden legs provide a stable base. The chair features nailhead trim along the bottom front edge, adding a decorative and functional element. The upholstery is a smooth, durable fabric, likely tweed or linen, in a solid gray color. The chair is symmetrical and presented against a plain black background.\", \"articulation_required\": false, \"plan\": {\"object_name\": \"Modern rounded upholstered armchair\", \"components\": [{\"name\": \"seat_base\", \"description\": \"Main upholstered chair body, centered at the origin and symmetric about the x=0 plane. Broad rounded rectangular volume in solid medium gray fabric, approximately 1.7 units wide (x), 1.0 unit deep (y), and 0.28 unit thick (z). Front faces toward -y. Corners and exposed edges should be softened using overlapping rounded primitives rather than remaining sharply box-like.\"}, {\"name\": \"seat_cushion\", \"description\": \"Thick ergonomic cushion resting on the seat base, approximately 1.35 units wide, 0.82 unit deep, and 0.20 unit thick. Use a rounded perimeter and smooth gray tweed/linen-like appearance. The sitting surface should read as slightly depressed at the center, with subtly higher side and front borders; this may be approximated with several blended rounded volumes or a shallow central subtraction.\"}, {\"name\": \"backrest\", \"description\": \"Tall upholstered back centered behind the seat on the +y side, approximately 1.55 units wide, 0.25–0.35 unit thick, and 1.15 units high above the seat. It should curve smoothly around the sitter: broad central back panel with rounded top corners and side portions that project slightly toward the front (-y). Solid gray upholstery matching the seat.\"}, {\"name\": \"left_armrest\", \"description\": \"Short upholstered arm on the -x side, rising approximately 0.35–0.45 units above the cushion. Rounded, compact elbow-rest form extending from near the backrest toward the front but stopping short of the seat's front edge. Its top should curve gently downward toward the front.\"}, {\"name\": \"right_armrest\", \"description\": \"Mirrored counterpart of the left armrest on the +x side, with identical size, curvature, height, and front-to-back placement.\"}, {\"name\": \"front_left_leg\", \"description\": \"Straight square wooden leg beneath the front-left corner (-x, -y). Slender rectangular prism, approximately 0.12–0.15 unit square and 0.55 unit tall. Warm medium-to-dark brown wood color.\"}, {\"name\": \"front_right_leg\", \"description\": \"Straight square wooden leg beneath the front-right corner (+x, -y), mirrored from the front-left leg.\"}, {\"name\": \"rear_left_leg\", \"description\": \"Straight square wooden leg beneath the rear-left corner (-x, +y), aligned vertically and matching the front legs in section, height, and wooden finish.\"}, {\"name\": \"rear_right_leg\", \"description\": \"Straight square wooden leg beneath the rear-right corner (+x, +y), mirrored from the rear-left leg.\"}, {\"name\": \"front_nailhead_trim\", \"description\": \"A single horizontal row of small, evenly spaced metallic hemispherical or spherical studs attached along the lower front edge of the upholstered seat base. Use roughly 13–17 small spheres, centered across x, all at the same z and slightly in front of the base on the -y side. Finish in muted silver, pewter, or dark nickel.\"}, {\"name\": \"upholstery_appearance\", \"description\": \"Uniform solid gray appearance applied to seat base, cushion, backrest, and both arms. Keep the surface visually smooth and durable; a fine tweed or linen impression may be suggested through color variation only if supported, without large patterns.\"}, {\"name\": \"background\", \"description\": \"Plain black presentation backdrop or ground environment, with no visible decorative objects. It should provide strong contrast while leaving the full chair silhouette readable.\"}], \"relations\": [\"Use world coordinates with +x to the chair's right, +y toward the rear/backrest, +z upward, and the visible front facing -y.\", \"The complete chair is bilaterally symmetrical across the vertical x=0 plane; left and right arms, legs, and trim spacing must mirror each other.\", \"The seat base forms the central structural body. Its underside is supported by all four legs, and its upper face supports the seat cushion.\", \"The seat cushion is centered left-to-right on the seat base and positioned slightly toward the front relative to the backrest. It must visibly contact the base without floating.\", \"The cushion's center is lower than its rounded outer border, producing a shallow ergonomic depression rather than a flat or deeply bowl-shaped seat.\", \"The backrest rises from and visually joins the rear (+y) portion of the seat base. Its lower edge should be partly obscured by or closely meet the rear edge of the cushion.\", \"The backrest curves around the seat in plan view: its center remains rearward while its left and right edges sweep slightly forward toward -y.\", \"Both armrests connect visually to the backrest and/or side portions of the seat base. They sit above the cushion edges but remain lower than the upper backrest.\", \"The armrests are intentionally short: their front ends terminate behind the seat cushion's front edge, leaving an open and inviting front profile.\", \"The four legs are vertical, straight, and square in section. Their tops meet the underside of the seat base near its four corners; their bottoms share one ground plane.\", \"Front legs are located toward -y and rear legs toward +y. Each left/right pair has equal x offsets from the centerline.\", \"The nailhead trim follows the lower front (-y) edge of the seat base, above and between the front legs. Stud centers are collinear along x and distributed with uniform center-to-center spacing.\", \"Nailheads protrude only slightly beyond the upholstery and remain much smaller than the legs or cushion details.\", \"Gray upholstery components should read as one coordinated shell and cushion assembly, while brown wooden legs and metallic trim provide material contrast.\", \"The chair should be centered against the black background and shown fully, with all four feet grounded and the silhouette unobstructed.\"], \"critic_checklist\": [\"Verify that the chair reads immediately as a modern upholstered armchair rather than a dining chair, sofa, or office chair.\", \"Confirm exact bilateral symmetry across x=0 for the major silhouette, armrests, leg placement, and nailhead row.\", \"Check that the front is consistently oriented toward -y and the backrest occupies the +y side.\", \"Ensure the overall form is rounded and ergonomic: no prominent sharp corners on the cushion, backrest, armrests, or upholstered base.\", \"Confirm the cushion has a visible but shallow central depression, with no hole, severe crease, or exaggerated bowl shape.\", \"Verify that the backrest rises substantially above the arms and has a smoothly rounded top and gently forward-curving side wings.\", \"Check that both armrests are short, curved, suitable for elbow support, and stop behind the cushion's front edge.\", \"Confirm the cushion, arms, and backrest intersect or contact the supporting body cleanly; reject visible floating gaps.\", \"Verify there are exactly four straight square-section wooden legs, one near each underside corner.\", \"Check that all four feet terminate on the same horizontal ground plane and that the chair appears stable.\", \"Ensure no legs pass visibly through the cushion or protrude above the upholstered seat base.\", \"Confirm that leg color is clearly brown and distinct from the solid gray upholstery.\", \"Verify the nailhead trim is confined to one evenly spaced horizontal row along the bottom front edge.\", \"Check that approximately 13–17 nailheads are present, equal in size, metallic in appearance, and centered between the front corners.\", \"Ensure the nailheads are decorative accents rather than oversized knobs and that they do not float away from the front upholstery.\", \"Confirm the upholstery is a consistent solid gray with no bold pattern, patchwork, or mismatched component colors.\", \"Check that the black background remains plain and does not obscure the dark wooden legs; maintain sufficient silhouette contrast.\", \"Inspect the final bounds to ensure the chair is centered, fully visible, upright, and not clipped by the presentation frame.\"]}, \"assignment\": \"Write source.py with the complete initial implementation.\"}"
